    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nPart of #38379. Re-enables `test_matryoshka` for `jinaai/jina-embeddings-v3` in `tests/models/language/pooling_mteb_test/test_jina.py`.\n\n**Depends on** the upstream fix to the model's remote code: https://huggingface.co/jinaai/xlm-roberta-flash-implementation/discussions/64. Until that is merged this test fails on `main` the same way it did when it was skipped, so this PR stays a draft.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `test_matryoshka` (HF Sentence Transformers vs vLLM embeddings with `dimensions`) runs again for jina-embeddings-v3.\n- Fixes the test's `dimensions` parametrization: `16` is not in the model's `matryoshka_dimensions` (`[32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 768, 1024]`), and since #48057 (merged while this test was skipped) vLLM rejects it with `VLLMValidationError`. The test now uses `32` and `64`.\n\n## Validation\n\nEnvironment: 1x RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, transformers 5.17.0, sentence-transformers 6.1.0, vLLM at this branch.\n\n```bash\npytest tests/models/language/pooling_mteb_test/test_jina.py -k test_matryoshka\n```\n\n| Remote code (`jinaai/xlm-roberta-flash-implementation`) | Result |\n|---|---|\n| current `main` | 2 failed: `AttributeError: 'XLMRobertaLoRA' object has no attribute 'all_tied_weights_keys'` |\n| with Hub PR #64 | **2 passed** (`dimensions=32`, `dimensions=64`), 4 skipped (not Matryoshka models) |\n\nWith the old `[16, 32]` parametrization and the Hub fix, `dimensions=32` passed and `dimensions=16` failed with `only supports Matryoshka dimensions [32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 768, 1024], got 16.`\n\nHub PR #64 was also checked outside vLLM: Sentence Transformers embeddings are bit-identical between transformers 4.57.6 (current code), 4.57.6 (patched) and 5.17.0 (patched).\n\n`pre-commit run --files tests/models/language/pooling_mteb_test/test_jina.py` passes.\n\n## Details\n\n- The skip was added in #30566. The root cause is in the checkpoint's remote code: `XLMRobertaLoRA.__init__` doesn't call `post_init()`. That is reported upstream in xlm-roberta-flash-implementation discussion #62, and Hub PR #64 fixes it.\n- Test-only change, no runtime code touched.\n- Duplicate check: no open vLLM PRs touch `test_jina.py`'s Matryoshka test or this skip.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR. (Claude Code was used for investigation, the change and running validation. I reviewed the change and the results.)\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
